! ax4b_2b_lhw_fullword.strap -- jb_ax4b "I-BOX 4", routine 148 (1248,
! "INDEX MODIFICATION TEST", banner PDF p.113), TEST 2B "CHECK IX MOD OF
! LHW OF FW INSTRCTN.":
!
!   PDF p.131  010263.40-010317.00  I4822: bits 0-2, exit
!   PDF p.132  010317.40-010353.00  I4823: bits 3-5, exit
!   PDF p.133  010353.40-010407.00  I4824: bits 6-8, exit
!   PDF p.134  010407.40-010443.00  I4825: bits 9-11, exit
!   PDF p.135  010443.40-010477.40  I4826: bits 12-14, exit (with a
!                                   second "BD,$+.32", as printed)
!   PDF p.136  010500.00-010533.00  I4827: bits 15-17, exit
!   PDF p.137  010533.40-010567.00  I4828: bits 18-20, exit
!   PDF p.138  010567.40-010623.00  I4829: bits 21-23, exit
!   PDF p.153  011351.00            148K24
!   PDF p.154  011374.00-011423.00  BIT0M-BIT23M
!   PDF p.191  013054.00-013103.00  BIT0-BIT23
!
! No printed page numbers on these sheets: cited by PDF page and octal
! location.  Read from the page images at 150 dpi; checked row for row
! against the printed machine code by
! tests/verify_ax4b_2b_lhw_fullword_listing.py.  p.131 carries pencil
! marks over the first block (ticks, "123456.76", "471370.0", an arrow
! at the L(BU) row); they are not IBM's code and are not transcribed.
!
! WHAT IT TESTS (IBM's code, unchanged).  For k = 0..23:
!   LVI,$X0,148K24; V+,$X0,BITk    X0's value := 148K24's address + bit k
!   LV,$X1,BIT(23-k)M              X1's value := -(bit k) (BITnM is the
!                                  index word -BIT(23-n), p.154)
!   SVA,$X0,$+.32                  X0's value INTO THE ADDRESS of
!   L(BU),0($X1)   0.00 81 000000.20 50   a full-word VFL indexed in its
!                                  LEFT half (I = 1): address + (-bit k)
!                                  must be 148K24 again
!   LX,$X1,$R; KV and KC vs 148K24     the word loaded must be 148K24's
! "ABOVE BIT WHEN SUBTRACTED THRU IX MOD FAILS TO YIELD CORRECT EFFECTIVE
! ADR."  Where 148K24's address already has bit k set, the V+ carries
! and the index subtraction must borrow back.
!
! EIGHT SEGMENTS, each ending in "B,SSW": I4822 ... I4829, three bits
! each.  The driver runs this deck eight times: from END (I4822) and
! with ENTRY=I4823 ... I4829 (gen_tb.py).  Continuity rows after each
! B,SSW are transcribed and verified, never run.
!
! SUBSTITUTIONS (not on these pages):
!   * SSIP's entry points: SSW (001301.00) is a PASS halt, SERS
!     (001304.00) a FAIL halt, SEN/SENO (001310.00/001311.00) data words
!     SIC stores into.  The addresses are the listing's own (B,SSW
!     prints "1301.10 00", B,SERS "1304.10 00", SIC,SEN "1310.00 80",
!     SIC,SENO+.32 "1311.40 80"); the contents are SSIP's, which is not
!     transcribed.  SIC "is executed if and only if the associated
!     branching is successful" (Reference Manual printed p.41, PDF 44),
!     so SEN stays 0 on a pass and names the error entry on a failure.
!   * IC248 is SYN'd from the printed "LX,$X13,IC248" (11306.32 10).
!   * BITnM: the page prints "XW,%8)-0.01" etc.; this assembler takes the
!     sign before the radix ("XW,-(8)0.01"), as ax5b_bit_table does for
!     100VO.  Notation only.
!   * Notation only: the page's "%" and the box glyph are "(" and ")";
!     the label glyph the scan shows as "1" is the letter I (I48..), as
!     for every ax4b label (docs/listing_typography.md).  Nothing else
!     changed.
!
! RESULT, 2026-11-19: every segment halts at SSW (PASS, PC 1410) with
! SEN = 0.  The driver compares PC, SEN, CYCLES and the pins listed in
! tests/run_tests.sh; CYCLES is MODEL BEHAVIOUR, not IBM's timing.
! SEN, on a failure, is SIC's link: the half-word after the "B,SERS" that
! was taken, so it names the failing check.
! MODEL INJECTIONS, OBSERVED (each built in its own scratch copy of
! stretch/bsv/, all 19 segment runs of TESTs 1-2 repeated; the
! worktree's bsv/ was never edited):
!   a negative index ADDS its magnitude (effAddrSigned's sign test
!     removed) -> all eight segments FAIL halt.  I4823 ... I4829 fail at
!     their first block (SEN 010327.40, 010363.40, 010417.40, 010453.40,
!     010507.40, 010543.40, 010577.40), CYCLES 214 (220 for I4829).
!     I4822 fails at its THIRD block, bit 2 (SEN 010313.40), CYCLES 580:
!     bits 0 and 1 pass anyway -- NOT TRACED.  INFERRED: the doubled
!     index carries out of the 24-bit address (bit 0, dropped per
!     pp.20-21) or reaches 2**23 (bit 1), where the read evidently still
!     yields 148K24's word.
!   I = 1..7 read X(I+8) (readIndex(idx | 8)) -> all eight FAIL halt at
!     their first block (I4822 SEN 010273.40, the others as above),
!     CYCLES 214 (220 for I4828, I4829).
!   I = 0 indexed by X0 (effAddrSigned's idx == 0 case removed) -> all eight
!     FAIL halt (PC 1416), CYCLES 204-214, SEN 0 (SIC,SEN is itself
!     indexed by X0 -- INFERRED as in TEST 1A).
!   CONTROL: the unmodified model in the same scratch arrangement: all
!     19 runs PASS with the pins in run_tests.sh.
!
! ---- SSIP's entry points: SUBSTITUTES (not on these pages) -----------
        SLC, (8)1301.0
SSW     BEW, $                        ! SUBSTITUTE: PASS (the return to SSIP)
        SLC, (8)1304.0
SERS    BEW, $                        ! SUBSTITUTE: FAIL (SSIP's error report)
        SLC, (8)1310.0
SEN     DD(BU,64,8), 0                ! SUBSTITUTE: SIC's error link word
SENO    DD(BU,64,8), 0                ! SUBSTITUTE: SIC's other link word
!
IC248   SYN, (8)11306.0
!
        SLC, (8)10263.40
! ======================================================================
! PDF p.131, 010263.40-010317.00
! ======================================================================
        CNOP                          ! -LH IX MODIFICATION, SUBTRACT BIT 0.
I4822   LVI, $X0, I48K24
        V+,  $X0, BIT0
        LV,  $X1, BIT23M
        NOP
        SVA, $X0, $+.32
        L(BU), 0($X1)
        LX,  $X1, $R
        KV,  $X1, I48K24
        BXE, $+1.0
        B,   $+1.32
        KC,  $X1, I48K24
        BXE, $+1.32
        SIC, SEN                      ! -ABOVE BIT WHEN SUBTRACTED THRU IX MOD
        B,   SERS                     ! -FAILS TO YIELD CORRECT EFFECTIVE ADR.
        CNOP                          ! -LH IX MODIFICATION, SUBTRACT BIT 1.
        LVI, $X0, I48K24
        V+,  $X0, BIT1
        LV,  $X1, BIT22M
        NOP
        SVA, $X0, $+.32
        L(BU), 0($X1)
        LX,  $X1, $R
        KV,  $X1, I48K24
        BXE, $+1.0
        B,   $+1.32
        KC,  $X1, I48K24
        BXE, $+1.32
        SIC, SEN                      ! -ABOVE BIT WHEN SUBTRACTED THRU IX MOD
        B,   SERS                     ! -FAILS TO YIELD CORRECT EFFECTIVE ADR.
        CNOP                          ! -LH IX MODIFICATION, SUBTRACT BIT 2.
        LVI, $X0, I48K24
        V+,  $X0, BIT2
        LV,  $X1, BIT21M
        NOP
        SVA, $X0, $+.32
        L(BU), 0($X1)
        LX,  $X1, $R
        KV,  $X1, I48K24
        BXE, $+1.0
        B,   $+1.32
        KC,  $X1, I48K24
        BXE, $+1.32
        SIC, SEN                      ! -ABOVE BIT WHEN SUBTRACTED THRU IX MOD
        B,   SERS                     ! -FAILS TO YIELD CORRECT EFFECTIVE ADR.
        B,   $+1.0
        BD,  I4822
        SIC, SENO+.32
        B,   SSW                      ! -TO SSIP.
        BD,  $+.32
        LX,  $X13, IC248              ! -UPDATE CONTINUITY.
        V+,  $X13, BIT11
        SX,  $X13, IC248
